<title>UK: NWE low sulphur straight-run fuel oil eases.</title>
<headline>NWE low sulphur straight-run fuel oil eases.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>NWE low sulphur straight-run fuel oil was steady to weaker on Tuesday and markets were still well supplied amid scant buying interest, traders said.</p>
<p>German quality material was still on offer and a regular buyer said he saw the offer at around $127 cif NWE.</p>
<p>Another regular buyer without any immediate requirements assessed the market at around $119 fob NWE.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 8167</p>
